{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-integral-stacks}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f441e75aa32bc7ed0ebf5b560753f4c5e83f49ce92c4ded60422dfa8b207df3", "source_text": "Integral algebraic stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb9859f6dc1fa0d183704d94dbe3a5473e5890e137dce2205d1e63863c733331", "unit_id": "tag:0GWA:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-over-fields-section-integral-spaces}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{proposition-decent-sober}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:90221730bba654112fe821593ce69acc884fbca24324eaf0f9c7ddaf6145f26c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the analogue of Spaces over Fields, Section\n<REF_0001>.\nMotivated by the considerations in that section and by the result\nof Proposition <REF_0002> we define an\nintegral algebraic stack as follows (and it does not conflict\nwith the already existing definitions of integral schemes and\nintegral algebraic spaces).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32b9863fce4a1465aee1cfcd82168ca6374bebf1ccc4784f61df681415a10f6f", "unit_id": "tag:0GWA:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-integral-algebraic-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:963246726c97a749366ee50690aed0a04e45fab35fbde9fa2f2f54c2eed1992b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3d0b38f5a4d4c8e5bc702b30fd729e8ba60c1e02ba76bfc3ac60c171a0ec47c9", "source_text": "We say an algebraic stack <MATH_0001> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>integral<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it is reduced, decent,\n<MATH_0002> is quasi-compact,\nand <MATH_0003> is irreducible.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:300a45e08c97326b288e7c446b6e7a78c6a960d4c497cbed24559577cf4a3af1", "unit_id": "tag:0GWB:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-totaro-case}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:086b218376c2256e72d0bf662883ce927920be3259d3f5b50e6eedd6163817ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bc739be3ade7489501202199c72b70bacec98359cf15fe3c77d9ace0b50ccf86", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that if <MATH_0001> is quasi-separated, then\nfor it to be integral, it suffices that <MATH_0002> is reduced\nand that <MATH_0003> is irreducible, see Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d4d3a40ad527e90a9c8f37e83fc6b70df71349979ded5581bfca707a8b06b9a5", "unit_id": "tag:0GWA:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-structure-integral-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:511ed693df79a44a324685a6a7fb7d3ecb2f67a24faf124d9b0fe1dacd0da527", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e30e70f941ecb2082b47d06b89ab92ee2389c7787b9827a7f7f0e0374d09c9c3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an integral algebraic stack. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is sober, irreducible, and has a unique generic point,\n<STRUCT_0003> there exists an open substack <MATH_0003> \nwhich is a gerbe over an integral scheme <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8c3f112d7d7dd4bc2d80d493f5802ba1f0989f2cf02c5fa20922390124dfce28", "unit_id": "tag:0GWC:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0007": "$|U| = |\\mathcal{U}|$", "MATH_0008": "$|U|$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to U$", "MATH_0011": "$U_{red}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to U$", "MATH_0013": "$U = U_{red}$", "MATH_0014": "$U$", "MATH_0015": "$U$", "MATH_0016": "$U$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0018": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-decent-sober}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{proposition-open-stratum}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-decent}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-representable-decent}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-map-into-reduction}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-fppf}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{spaces-over-fields-definition-integral-algebraic-space}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{spaces-over-fields-section-integral-spaces}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a2aaccf25c5a715a5c92eec905833941c376161905404e92fff9d6aace1cc9c9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b82bfab9a9c18c3748eac68e125dc61e2e306c2dee0baa5c10d3aa042c818d0b", "source_text": "Proposition <REF_0001> tells us that <MATH_0001>\nis sober. Of course it is also irreducible and hence has a unique generic\npoint <MATH_0002> (by the definition of sobriety).\nProposition <REF_0002> shows\nthe existence of a dense open <MATH_0003>\nwhich is a gerbe over an algebraic space <MATH_0004>.\nThen <MATH_0005> is a decent algebraic space by\nLemma <REF_0003> (and the fact that <MATH_0006>\nis decent by Lemma <REF_0004>).\nSince <MATH_0007> we see that <MATH_0008> is irreducible.\nFinally, since <MATH_0009> is reduced the morphism\n<MATH_0010> factors through <MATH_0011>, see\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0005>.\nNow since <MATH_0012> is flat, locally of finite presentation,\nand surjective (Lemma <REF_0006>), this implies that\n<MATH_0013>, i.e., <MATH_0014> is reduced (small detail omitted).\nIt follows that <MATH_0015> is an integral algebraic space, see\nSpaces over Fields, Definition\n<REF_0007>.\nThen finally, we may replace <MATH_0016> (and correspondingly <MATH_0017>)\nby an open subspace and assume that <MATH_0018> is an integral scheme, see\ndiscussion in  Spaces over Fields, Section\n<REF_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5be42864722ad0d6bde462b24bbcd94d6c860d40a6ea2e412545ee91995d4e0f", "unit_id": "tag:0GWC:proof"}
